{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Extend the Mule connector framework to include dedicated WebSocket inbound and outbound endpoint components that use an underlying NIO transport stack, toggleable via deploy.properties.",
    "Develop a Registry integration module that securely stores the registry key, listens to application lifecycle events, and registers/manages HTTP endpoints with the configured Registry instance.",
    "Implement a Dynamic Router message processor capable of dynamically resolving dynamic endpoints against the Registry service at runtime.",
    "Create a runtime throttling policy filter/interceptor component applied to Mule endpoints as specified by Registry policies.",
    "Extend the event tracking and logging framework to intercept custom business events and transaction IDs and format them for stdout/log files during application execution.",
    "Upgrade MVEL dependency in Maven build files to 2.1.8 and execute regression tests across DataMapper and Mule expression evaluators.",
    "Extend database connector metadata and default configurations to support connection templates for Oracle, PostgreSQL, Sybase, MS SQL Server, and DB2.",
    "Implement a JDBC statement wrapper/interceptor that checks log level configuration and logs execute SQL queries when set to DEBUG."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Registry API specifications for authentication, endpoint registration, endpoint lookup, and policy retrieval are available via internal documentation.",
    "Database drivers for target vendors (Oracle, PostgreSQL, Sybase, MS SQL Server, DB2) are available in accessible repositories for integration testing.",
    "Development and testing will be performed by a single developer with strong familiarity with Mule ESB architecture.",
    "Effort estimates include design, implementation, unit testing, integration testing, and technical documentation updates."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-1",
      "activity_name": "NIO Stack Toggle & WebSocket Component Implementation (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Add support for reading NIO configuration from deploy.properties, implement NIO transport hooks, and create WebSocket flow components (inbound/outbound).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-2",
      "activity_name": "Registry Account Pairing & HTTP Endpoint Management (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement registry key configuration handling and deploy-time lifecycle listener to automatically register and manage deployed application HTTP endpoints with the Registry.",
      "most_likely_effort": 9
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-3",
      "activity_name": "Dynamic Lookup Component Implementation (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Build the dynamic router flow component supporting dynamic endpoint lookup and resolution through the paired Registry API.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-4",
      "activity_name": "Throttling Policies Enforcement (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Develop endpoint interceptor components to enforce throttling policies defined in and retrieved from the Registry.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-5",
      "activity_name": "Custom Business Events & Transaction ID Logging (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Enhance event notifications to extract and format custom business events and transaction IDs to Mule system logs during local development.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-6",
      "activity_name": "MVEL Upgrade to 2.1.8 & Compatibility Validation (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Update MVEL dependencies to version 2.1.8, adapt DataMapper and expression parsing layers as needed, and verify expression evaluation stability.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-7",
      "activity_name": "Multi-Database JDBC Connectivity Configurations (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Add out-of-the-box configuration helpers and connection providers for Oracle, PostgreSQL, Sybase, MS SQL Server, and DB2.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-8",
      "activity_name": "DEBUG Mode SQL Query Logging (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a query interceptor in the database transport layer to output full SQL statements to standard Mule logs when log level is set to DEBUG.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-9",
      "activity_name": "Integration Testing and Release Preparation",
      "activity_description": "Conduct end-to-end integration testing across all updated subsystems, resolve regression issues, and prepare documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 52
  }
}
```

